A||||1||Jim's87GT||Oil leak at the transmission dipstick?||||5||
Z||000000||Jim's87GT||10-05-2000||07:54 PM||||I've been trying to chace down the leaks from my car engine.  The transmission pan gasket was a BIG source of "drips" and the drain plug washer on the motor oil pan was shot and that being replased helped a lot.  Now I have a tiny drip that seems to be coming from the area where the dipstick for the automatic transmission bolts to the case.  Has anyone ever chased a leak to this spot.  I'm reluctant to fool with it before getting advise from you guys.  Is there a gasket at this location?  Hints?  Thanks Guys||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||10-05-2000||08:07 PM||||There's an o ring on the dip tube. unfasten the tube and carfully work it out of the tranny. replace the o ring, oil the ring and shove it back in the hole.||||reg||1
